From 65637339ed409825bc406d5bbd3cfcd6ac164fcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Brandon Barclay (AK6MJ)" <ak6mj@w7avm.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:43:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Make the PTT button, and the Space bar, hold-to-talk

The PTT button toggled the transmitter on each click, so a missed second
click left the radio keyed. It now transmits only while held.

- Pointer down keys the radio ({"ptt", state:true, hold:true}); the page
  then sends a keepalive every 500 ms; pointer up, pointer cancel, losing
  pointer capture, the window losing focus, or the tab being hidden all
  release. Requests are strictly ordered, so a release can never overtake
  the key-down, and at most one keepalive is queued.
- The Space bar does the same, but not while typing in a field. Key
  auto-repeat is ignored and its default action (scrolling the page) is
  suppressed.
- The button looks pressed immediately and goes back if the radio refuses.
- If the browser has no microphone (see "RX only, NO MIC") keying shows the
  reason instead of silently transmitting a carrier with nothing on it.

The server side is the watchdog from the previous commits: if the page
dies mid-transmit, the radio unkeys within about 1.5 s.

Checked in headless Chrome against this branch's own files and a mock
radio, logging what the page sends: holding the button for 1.3 s sent one
key-down, two keepalives and one release, then nothing; Space with an
auto-repeat sent one key-down, keepalives and one release; a window blur
while keyed released; Space inside a text field sent nothing. I have not
yet exercised this exact branch on the radio.
